<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n67436" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηλο-σφᾰγέω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>slay sheep</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱερὰ μ.</span>
			<i>offer sheep</i> in sacrifice, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				280
			</span></i>: abs., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. δαιμόνων ἐπ᾽ ἐσχάραις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					628
				</span></i>
			: generally, <i>offer sacrifice</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βουθύτοις ἐπ᾽ ἐσχάραις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Av.</u>
					1232
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>Abst.</u>
				1.57
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. εἰς ἀσπίδα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Lys.</u>
					189
				</span></i>
			 (hence perh. to be read in <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				43
			</span></i> for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταυροσφ</span>-): comically,
				<i>offer</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἴνου σταμνίον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Lys.</u>
					196
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
